## 1. Introduction

### 1.1 Welcome to BrightPath

Welcome to BrightPath Analytics! We are a B2B SaaS company dedicated to helping small and mid-sized retailers make smarter business decisions through data-driven insights, customizable dashboards, and AI-powered analytics. Our 45-member team works across product engineering, customer success, data analytics, sales, and business operations from our Bengaluru headquarters and Mumbai sales office.

We believe that great companies are built by great people. This handbook is designed to help you understand how BrightPath operates, what you can expect from us, and what we expect from you in terms of professional conduct, performance, and collaboration.

### 1.2 Purpose of This Handbook

This Employee Handbook outlines:
- Company values, mission, and culture
- Employment practices and classifications
- Working hours, attendance, and remote work policies
- Leave and holiday entitlements
- Code of conduct and workplace behavior standards
- Workplace safety and security protocols
- Data protection and acceptable use of company assets
- Compensation, benefits, and performance review processes
- Discipline and grievance procedures
- Separation and exit processes

This handbook is not a contract of employment. All employment at BrightPath is at-will, meaning either the employee or the company may terminate the relationship at any time for any lawful reason, with or without cause, and with or without notice, except as required by applicable law.

### 1.3 At-Will Employment and Policy Updates

BrightPath reserves the right to modify, supplement, or eliminate any provision of this handbook at any time. The most current version of this handbook is maintained in the HR portal and supersedes all previous versions. Employees will be notified of material changes via email and in-person briefings where applicable.

