## 7. Workplace Safety and Security

### 7.1 Health and Safety Basics

All employees must comply with health and safety protocols to protect themselves and colleagues:

- Familiarize yourself with emergency exits, assembly points, and evacuation procedures upon joining.
- Follow posted safety instructions in office spaces, including those related to fire safety, electrical safety, and first aid.
- Immediately report any accidents, injuries, hazards, near-misses, or security incidents to the office administrator or HR.
- Do not operate machinery or equipment without proper training and authorization.
- Keep workspaces free of clutter and ensure cables and furniture do not create trip hazards.

**Emergency Procedures**:
- In case of fire, evacuate immediately using the nearest exit and proceed to the assembly point.
- In case of medical emergency, contact the office admin immediately; they will call emergency services.
- In case of security threats (break-in, unauthorized access), lock doors, move to a safe room, and contact security and police.

### 7.2 Ergonomics and Remote Work Safety

Employees working from home or in the office should maintain ergonomic practices to prevent injury:

- Use an ergonomic chair with back support; adjust the height so your feet rest flat on the ground
- Position your monitor at eye level, approximately 50-70 cm (20-28 inches) from your eyes
- Keep your keyboard and mouse at elbow height
- Take short breaks every 60-90 minutes; stand, stretch, and look away from the screen
- Report any ergonomic issues or physical discomfort to your manager and HR

For remote employees, the company provides guidance on setting up a home office and may approve reimbursement for ergonomic equipment (e.g., chairs, standing desks) with manager approval and documentation.

### 7.3 Access, Badges, and Security

- All employees receive a personalized access card for office entry. Keep your card secure and do not share it with others.
- If your access card is lost or misplaced, report it to the office administrator within 24 hours so it can be deactivated immediately.
- Replacement cards incur a fee of INR 500, which may be charged back depending on circumstances.
- Visitors and contractors must be registered with the office admin and accompanied at all times while on company premises.
- Do not hold doors open for unauthorized individuals or allow them to tailgate into secure areas.
- Suspicious activity or unauthorized access attempts should be reported to the office admin immediately.

