## 9. Compensation and Benefits

### 9.1 Pay Cycles and Payroll

- All regular salaries are paid monthly via direct bank transfer.
- Payroll is processed and transferred on or before the last working day of each month.
- Salary slips are generated and made available in the HRIS portal by the 25th of each month.
- Deductions from salary include provident fund contributions, income tax (TDS), professional tax (if applicable), and any voluntary deductions authorized by the employee (e.g., loan repayments, charity donations).

### 9.2 Performance Reviews and Salary Revisions

**Annual Performance Review**:
- All employees receive a formal performance review annually, typically in November-December.
- Mid-year check-ins occur in May-June to discuss progress toward goals and address any performance concerns early.
- Performance reviews are based on:
  - Achievement of individual goals and OKRs
  - Demonstration of company values
  - Quality of work and delivery
  - Collaboration and teamwork
  - Learning and development

**Salary Revisions**:
- Salary revisions are linked to performance ratings, business results, and market benchmarks for roles.
- Not all employees receive a salary increase each year; increases depend on performance and company financial health.
- Any salary revisions take effect on April 1st each year, with formal communication by March 31st.
- Promotions and role changes may result in immediate salary adjustments as per policy.

### 9.3 Benefits Overview

**Health Insurance**:
- Full-time regular employees are covered under a comprehensive health insurance plan.
- Coverage includes the employee and eligible dependents (spouse and children, as defined by the insurance policy).
- The company bears the full premium cost; employees pay no monthly deduction.
- Coverage includes in-patient hospitalization, emergency services, and optional outpatient coverage.
- Details of coverage, network hospitals, and claim procedures are available in the HR portal and from the HR department.

**Provident Fund (PF)**:
- Full-time regular employees are enrolled in the Employees' Provident Fund Organization (EPFO) as per the Employees' Provident Funds and Miscellaneous Provisions Act, 1952.
- Employee contribution: 12% of basic salary (deducted from salary)
- Employer contribution: 12% of basic salary (paid by the company)
- Provident fund is a retirement savings account that grows with interest and can be partially withdrawn for specific purposes (e.g., home purchase, higher education) or fully withdrawn upon retirement.

**Learning and Development Budget**:
- Each full-time regular employee receives an annual learning budget of INR 40,000 for courses, certifications, conferences, or books.
- Budget is allocated per fiscal year and does not carry over to the next year if unused.
- Learning must be relevant to the employee's role or career development path.
- Approval from the manager is required before enrollment; the employee should submit a brief justification (course title, provider, cost, expected outcome).

**Other Benefits**:
- Flexible leave: Casual leave can be taken for personal reasons with manager approval.
- Remote work: Eligible employees can work from home with manager and VP approval.
- Discounts: Employees may be eligible for discounts on third-party products/services through BrightPath's partnerships (details in HR portal).
- Wellness: The company may offer wellness programs, fitness benefits, or mental health support based on annual decisions.

